    "result_text": "The full suite ran green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ownerSegment` (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **New cohesive class** `service/OwnerSegment.java` \u2014 a single small static method holding all the new logic. TIER is `PREMIUM` when the effective `membershipLevel` (explicit value, else derived via `MembershipLevel.of`) is \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when the region (customerCode prefix) is in `{NSW, VIC, QLD}`, else `REGIONAL`. It mirrors the existing `RegionTimezone`/`MembershipLevel` idioms, so WMC_other is ~0 and its CC is low.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`; no existing method body was touched (the changed method stays CC 1, one changed line).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` schema field so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nNo existing methods grew and no logic was piled into a large class \u2014 the behaviour lives in its own tiny unit.",
